  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\r\n\r\nConsider invoking `stepDown` for  `<input type=time max=17:00 step=900>`. Blink sets the value to 00:00 while Gecko computes 23:45.\r\n\r\nAccording to [stepDown](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-input-stepdown), we subtract 15 minutes from zero obtaining a negative value. The element has no minimum and -00:15 is less than 17:00. In step 11 we then determine the new element value as\r\n> a valid time string that represents the time that is input milliseconds after midnight on a day with no time changes\r\n\r\nsee [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#time-state-(type=time):concept-input-value-number-string).\r\n\r\nMaybe time input elements should have a [default minimum](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-input-min-default) of zero and default maximum of 23:59?",
